From: openEuler RISC-V packaging maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid competing string copy and move conversions

GCC 14 compiling the unchanged original test_text_reader.cpp fails on
line = reader: conversion to both string and const string& makes the copy
and move assignment candidates ambiguous. Keep the implicit const string&
conversion: it still supports reference binding, string copy construction
and assignment, including the exact failing original expression. Remove only
the redundant by-value conversion overload, not a test or assertion. The
explicit line_string/line_stream methods and implicit stream conversion
are unchanged. A direct named call to operator std::string() is no longer
available; consumers should copy the implicit reference or line_string().
This is an upstream-generic C++11-and-later compatibility change, not a
RISC-V-specific fix. Confirmed failure: Package CI 38793276327, exact head
0a8eb781445958fbdb95ae5f4e9b6dacb2b08453. Remove when upstream supplies an
equivalent unambiguous conversion interface.
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (no upstream write authorized)
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later

--- a/src/gtextutils/text_line_reader.h
+++ b/src/gtextutils/text_line_reader.h
@@ -57 +56,0 @@
-	operator std::string() const { return line_string(); }
